msgid "RC control (not enabled by default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:19
#: 2a5d2495eab94dc2b999f56b747ecf5e
msgid "Pilot Control Inputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:20
#: 7446d2524bdc43319c22f2b836d50f8e
msgid "If RC is not enabled, pilot inputs are via the GCS joystick, controlling the vehicle's available motion axes, including yaw and attitude rotations, along with body-frame translations laterally, forward/back, and up/down in depth. Additionally, lights and camera can be controlled from the GCS, as well as some generic servo and/or relay outputs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:22
#: ccf286d888ab425b92aadc890905a509
msgid "If RC is enabled, then the pitch/roll/yaw/throttle/lateral/forward inputs are sent from the RC transmitter and mapped from RC channels to these inputs via the ``RCMAP_`` parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:25
#: 4beafbafcfac408ebf4d15a485a2b971
msgid "Pilot Control Freedoms by Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:26
#: 84ef3b5b0b344b869dfe4aed41e36f2f
msgid "The following assumes the axis is controllable. Some frame configurations do not provide all axes. For example the SimpleROV-3 frame has three thrusters providing only yaw, forward, and depth control. The pitch and roll attitude is uncontrolled and relies on CG/ballast trimming and has no lateral movement capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:28
#: 7274da4c9a4e4ebd9906a19e3fd03828
msgid "ANG = Angle target. Stick deflection indicates desired axis angle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:30
#: b89d77a9a7f24076a484c3816b29f619
msgid "RAT = Rate target. Stick deflection indicates desired axis movement/rotation rate."
