#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:63
#: b6acc840d657492085de2633a9cc7e9a
msgid "Responsiveness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:64
#: 1dd5bc3451bd44568ca823953d72a727
msgid "Depending on vehicle design and pilot experience, it can be desirable to limit how quickly and/or strongly the vehicle responds to control inputs. There are a few different approaches to doing this, which affect different parts of the control pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:66
#: 12bd13f6170547eda4f584128b3752f0
msgid "If a GCS joystick is used, the ``JS_GAIN_*`` parameters scale the pilot input range, which determines  how much pilot joystick inputs can affect motor outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:68
#: 35cf2aeace164c70bb11ec1f8543be71
msgid "In MANUAL mode there are only pilot inputs, so the total output range (and hence power usage) of the vehicle is determined by the pilot's input control range, whether GCS joystick based or RC based"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:69
#: fa078037201242f58c75a127cd3d70b0
msgid "In modes with autopilot stabilisation, stabilisation can still cause the vehicle to use its full power capacity (e.g. when operating in strong currents)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:70
#: e637849484cf40eb9417f5efa9e73d90
msgid "Joystick gain can be controlled by the pilot using ``gain_*`` :ref:`buttons`, and/or can be configured with the parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:72
#: c920e69443f445648ef45aea8c7a73ef
msgid ":ref:`JS_GAIN_MIN<JS_GAIN_MIN>`, :ref:`JS_GAIN_MAX<JS_GAIN_MAX>`, and :ref:`JS_GAIN_DEFAULT<JS_GAIN_DEFAULT>` for its limits and starting value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:73
#: c35e35ba9aab4ab1809b0966b78e72ec
msgid ":ref:`JS_THR_GAIN<JS_THR_GAIN>` for an additional scaling applied to vertical inputs, to either reduce them further or boost them relative to horizontal/turning inputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:74
#: eb550daabfc442de997787493d598773
msgid ":ref:`JS_GAIN_STEPS<JS_GAIN_STEPS>` to determine how much the gain changes with each increment/decrement button press"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:75
#: 653a7598ead34b748ff463b0a1ab31e2
msgid "When using radio channels for RC control of the vehicle, it is possible to ignore small RC stick adjustments and timing inconsistencies using :ref:`RCn_DZ<RC1_DZ>` to specify the deadzone for each RC channel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:76
#: 3f4775fd9c4646f4be9cc6538aa87d8e
msgid "Attitude stabilisation limits the vehicle's maximum lean angle (roll/pitch away from level) to :ref:`ATC_ANGLE_MAX<ATC_ANGLE_MAX>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:77
#: f1db5b1be1214f48aaa1ed61af41a46c
msgid "Automatic depth control (in modes like ALT_HOLD, SURFTRAK, POSHOLD, and CIRCLE) can be configured with the parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:79
#: 782872152bd24f849ca53215d8e8e133
msgid ":ref:`THR_DZ<THR_DZ>` for the throttle deadzone, to avoid small joystick movements adjusting the current depth target"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:80
#: 86cfeeab16c143388ed206e2481b9791
msgid ":ref:`PILOT_SPD_UP<PILOT_SPD_UP>` and :ref:`PILOT_ACC_Z<PILOT_ACC_Z>`, for limiting maximum vertical speeds, and setting the vertical acceleration to reach those speeds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:82
#: bd7c0d4c8ba24aa5b04463b50148a522
msgid ":ref:`PILOT_SPD_DN<PILOT_SPD_DN>` can be optionally used to set the maximum descent rate independently, instead of defaulting to :ref:`PILOT_SPD_UP<PILOT_SPD_UP>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:83
#: fc0d3a4f8ce240d2a1197f89f7c3671a
msgid ":ref:`SURFACE_MAX_THR<SURFACE_MAX_THR>` scales down upwards thrust when near the surface, to avoid pushing through the water surface and sucking air"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:84
#: e437dbdcfd204396bd45cb7307e0ea99
msgid "Automatic horizontal velocity control in POSHOLD mode can be limited by :ref:`PILOT_SPEED<PILOT_SPEED>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:85
#: f104efae45ca49d0b7aa91e348fd70a6
msgid "It is also possible to configure the outputs directly, using"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:87
#: 18886b817abf4db9b77437270e1c3659
msgid ":ref:`MOT_SLEW_UP_TIME<MOT_SLEW_UP_TIME>` and :ref:`MOT_SLEW_DN_TIME<MOT_SLEW_DN_TIME>`, to limit the rate the motors can increase or decrease thrust levels when a change is commanded"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:88
#: 3a668c674f6f483fa604928c986d33f6
msgid ":ref:`MOT_PWM_MIN<MOT_PWM_MIN>` and :ref:`MOT_PWM_MAX<MOT_PWM_MAX>` define the available PWM range of all motor outputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:90
#: adcf5012c56c4395b94589eabbf679a2
msgid "This is typically used to ensure the motor output commands match the expected input range of the ESCs, but can also be used to intentionally set a reduced range, to reduce performance and/or power usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:92
#: ed2fc79929374d3494bf72c8fb8e59a9
msgid "Dshot ESCs ignore these values. Range is fixed at 1000µs to 2000µs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:94
#: af4bb5879e2d4a1894d890da6a1f9dff
msgid "If one or more PWM ESC controlled motors are moving while disarmed, it may be necessary to adjust the relevant :ref:`SERVOn_TRIM<SERVO1_TRIM>` parameter(s) to correct the neutral points"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:95
#: 28c5ab77cc264c109f73e0e143b7695f
msgid "Motor output scaling can also be adjusted automatically, :ref:`in response to feedback from the power/battery monitoring system <current-limiting-and-voltage-scaling>`, using"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:97
#: 3c85a3f1d0334402b25f7d67cc78b45f
msgid ":ref:`MOT_BAT_CURR_MAX<MOT_BAT_CURR_MAX>` to reduce the power output after excessive current draw occurs for more than :ref:`MOT_BAT_CURR_TC<MOT_BAT_CURR_TC>`, and/or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/pilot-control.rst:98
#: 3abb13da67b243488fa88b5cb09b5267
msgid ":ref:`MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN<MOT_BAT_VOLT_MIN>` and :ref:`MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX<MOT_BAT_VOLT_MAX>` to scale up motor outputs to compensate for sagging voltage over time"
msgstr ""
